 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Every element has a symbol of one or two letters. The first letter is a capital; the second is small: H hydrogen, He helium, C carbon, Ca calcium, Cl chlorine.\nMost symbols come from the English name. Some come from the Latin name: Na sodium (natrium), K potassium (kalium), Fe iron (ferrum), Cu copper (cuprum), Ag silver (argentum), Pb lead (plumbum), Au gold (aurum), Hg mercury (hydrargyrum), Sn tin (stannum).\nThe first 20 elements, in order: H, He, Li, Be, B, C, N, O, F, Ne, Na, Mg, Al, Si, P, S, Cl, Ar, K, Ca.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "a": "Co",
   "b": "CO"
  },
  "problem": "Explain the difference between {a} and {b}.",
  "steps": [
   "{a}: one capital and one small letter, so one symbol: cobalt, an element.",
   "{b}: two capitals, so two symbols: C (carbon) and O (oxygen), the compound carbon monoxide."
  ],
  "answer": "{a} is the element cobalt; {b} is a compound of carbon and oxygen.",
  "checks": []
 },
